WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
Michel de Nostradame, AKA Nostradamus
By Arnaldo Teodorani

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.080
Intro
[A slightly different intro here, with words

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:03.080
appearing on screen against a dark background,
as Simon read them]

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:04.080
From “Les Propheties”, Century nr XIII,
Quatraine nr LXXII

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.080
Anné dix-nouef la Terre est fatiguée
Un marteau de tenebre comme peste tombera

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.080
Des mains du Prince des mille fenetres, argentées
Puis seul et Roi des décombres, il rira,

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.080
l’homme qui siffle
I hope you did pardon my French.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.080
My name is Simon, Simon Whistler [TA1] and
that was the quatraine number 72, from ‘Century’

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.080
- or chapter - nr 13 of The Prophecies, written
in 1555 by the most famous, most quoted and

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.080
most accurate visionary prophet of modern
times.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.960
A French doctor, pharmacist, alchemist and
practitioner of the occult who in his lifetime

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.660
would advise Royalty and who after death would
never be out of print.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:24.539
He is our protagonist of today: Michel De
Nostradame, better known as Nostradamus.

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:36.560
There

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.150
is little that we know with certainty about
his life and exploits, but we will trace his

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:44.520
career and look in detail at some of his most
famous prophecies.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:48.260
And, as it is fitting for such a mysterious
character, there is more to be discovered

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:52.430
about Nostradamus and his prophecies, as proven
by the recent finding of a Century nr 13 in

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:55.270
the old library of his alma mater, the University
of Montpellier.

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:59.970
A chapter a pparently entirely dedicated to
the End of Times, from which we have quoted

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:02.800
the early quatrain … but more on this later.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:08.370
For the moment, let’s dive into Nostradamus’
formative years.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:16.070
Early Life
Michel de Nostradame was born in Saint-Remy-de-Provence,

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:21.030
southern France, either on the 14th or the
21st of December 1503 to parents Reyniere

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:26.290
de St-Remy, and her husband Jaume de Nostradame,
who worked as a grain dealer and notary.

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:31.220
Michel’s grandfather, Guy Gassonet, was
a Jewish doctor and Kabbalist who had converted

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:36.540
to Catholicism in 1455 and changed the family
name to Nostradame, as a means to avoid discrimination

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:39.480
and even persecution by the Inquisition.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:43.890
We don’t know much about Michel’s childhood,
except that he was very bright and that he

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:45.190
advanced quickly through school.

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:49.880
Both of his grandfathers recognised his potential
for learning and dedicated themselves to tutoring

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:50.880
him.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.880
His maternal grandfather, Jean de St Remy
taught him how to speak and read in Latin,

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.680
Greek, Hebrew, as well as the rudiments of
mathematics.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:02.880
While his paternal grandad, Guy the Kabbalist,
introduced him to the more exoteric knowledge

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.920
of ancient Jewish tradition and the science
of astrology.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.950
Although this has been disputed, it could
explain Nostradame’s interest in applying

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:15.060
the study of celestial bodies and how they
could influence human destiny.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:23.480
Studies
At the precocious age of 14, Nostradame signed

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:27.200
up to the University of Avignon to study medicine.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:31.430
His studies were cut short the following year,
however, because of an outbreak of the bubonic

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:32.430
plague.

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:35.350
This may have been his first encounter with
the deadly epidemic, to which he dedicated

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:40.459
most of his medical practice in later years
In the following four years young Michel travelled

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:45.510
the French countryside researching herbal
remedies and working as an apothecary.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:50.550
In 1522, aged 19, he gave it another go at
getting a degree, this time entering the University

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:54.599
of Montpelier, at that time regarded as one
of the best for the teaching of medicine.

00:02:54.599 --> 00:02:59.431
The faculty was largely composed of Catholic
priests, with whom he clashed often.

00:02:59.431 --> 00:03:04.840
Apparently they were dismissive or even suspicious
of his early astrological knowledge.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.750
Let’s not forget that this was a period
of great religious tension in the French Kingdom

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:13.710
with the Protestant faction of the Huguenots
growing in power both in the South and in

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:19.650
the Parisian court, causing the Catholic establishment
to be suspicious of any ‘heretic’ believer,

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:22.050
including those who had Jewish origins.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:27.300
But what ultimately led to his expulsion from
medical school was a more mundane matter:

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:31.750
university officials found out about his previous
trade as an apothecary, something considered

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:37.420
as a lesser ‘manual trade’ and therefore
unworthy of that lofty temple of medical studies

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:38.890
that was Montpelier.

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:43.420
This approach is consistent with views of
the time, in fact even surgeons were considered

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:47.900
manual labourers and treated as “2nd class
citizens” by medical professionals.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:50.970
But was he actually expelled, though?

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:55.030
After all, surgeons were allowed to attend
lectures in Montpelier, even though they had

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:59.709
to buy – or even steal - their own corpses
if they wanted to practice with their scalpels.[TA2]

00:03:59.709 --> 00:04:03.360
And in fact, other accounts state that Michel
De Nostradame did complete his medical degree

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:08.680
in 1525, the same year in which he changed
his name to the Latin ‘Nostradamus’, as

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:12.550
was common practice among intellectuals and
academics of the time.

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.980
But did he actually get a degree, though?

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:20.019
Now, according to other accounts, it was during
the years 1521 to 1529 that we travelled the

00:04:20.019 --> 00:04:24.189
countryside perfecting his herbal remedies
and apothecary skills.

00:04:24.189 --> 00:04:28.909
In those years Nostradamus was aged 18 to
26 years old, the age in which one would normally

00:04:28.909 --> 00:04:30.139
go to University.

00:04:30.139 --> 00:04:34.349
As I mentioned earlier, there is little certainty
on Nostradamus’ earlier life.

00:04:34.349 --> 00:04:38.789
But what it matters is that he did acquire
medical knowledge, either through study or

00:04:38.789 --> 00:04:43.759
through hands-on practice, and that he would
use that knowledge against the bane of his

00:04:43.759 --> 00:04:46.379
contemporaries, the bubonic plague.

00:04:46.379 --> 00:04:55.259
The Plague Doctor
Over the end of the 1520s and early 1530s,

00:04:55.259 --> 00:04:57.180
Nostradamus married and had two children.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:01.879
He was frequently travelling, however, especially
around Southern France and Italy, treating

00:05:01.879 --> 00:05:03.710
victims of the bubonic plague.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:07.779
There was no known treatment at the time for
this infectious disease, but Nostradamus had

00:05:07.779 --> 00:05:12.919
a stab at developing a healing powder:
‘Take one ounce of the sawdust of cypress-wood,

00:05:12.919 --> 00:05:18.699
as green as you can find, six ounces of Florentine
violet-root, three ounces of cloves, three

00:05:18.699 --> 00:05:24.419
drams of sweet calamus, and six drams of aloes-wood’
Did it work?

00:05:24.419 --> 00:05:33.430
We know that violet-root is still used today
to treat cough and fevers, so maybe yes.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:34.430
Although … calamus?

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:37.960
It is forbidden in the US because of its toxicity!

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:39.499
So maybe, not.

00:05:39.499 --> 00:05:45.330
But: what Nostradamus did get right were the
methods to prevent outbreaks of plague: effective

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:49.300
personal hygiene, removal of infected corpses,
fresh air.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:54.860
Simple stuff today, but pretty revolutionary
for XVI Century Europe.

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:58.979
Thanks to these measures Nostradamus became
a local celebrity in the Provence region,

00:05:58.979 --> 00:06:02.220
in Southern France, even receiving financial
support from its citizens.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:07.430
And in 1531, Jules-Cesar Scaliger, a leading
physician of his time, became his patron and

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:11.139
invited him to work with him in Agen, in southwestern
France.

00:06:11.139 --> 00:06:12.719
But the plague did not rest.

00:06:12.719 --> 00:06:17.909
Here is, in Nostradamus’ own words, a vivid
description of a common sight at that time

00:06:17.909 --> 00:06:21.680
"Among the [most] admirable things I saw,
was a woman who, even while I was calling

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:26.279
to her through the window, replied to what
I was saying while sewing herself unaided

00:06:26.279 --> 00:06:29.270
into her own shroud, starting with the feet."

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:33.460
She was later found dead in the middle of
the house - "with her sewing half-finished".

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:38.639
In 1534, Nostradamus’ own wife and children
died, presumably of the plague, while he was

00:06:38.639 --> 00:06:40.509
on a medical mission in Italy.

00:06:40.509 --> 00:06:44.639
In addition to being a personal tragedy, this
was a blow to his own reputation of plague

00:06:44.639 --> 00:06:51.409
doctor, which caused him to fall out of favour
with both the community and his patron, Scaliger.

00:06:51.409 --> 00:06:57.520
An Occult Awakening
In the years following the death of his family,

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:01.819
Nostradamus started to move away from medicine
and towards occult practices, most notably

00:07:01.819 --> 00:07:03.929
astrology and divination.

00:07:03.929 --> 00:07:08.460
According to legend – which unfortunately
is all we have – in 1538 he was forced to

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:11.210
leave France after a brush with the Inquisition.

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:15.150
During his travels in Italy he came across
a young Franciscan friar called Felice [Fell-ee-tche]

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:17.559
in front of whom he immediately knelt down.

00:07:17.559 --> 00:07:22.289
Years later, the friar was to become Pope
Sixtus V. Nostradamus also journeyed across

00:07:22.289 --> 00:07:27.190
Greece and Turkey, picking up more occult
knowledge and experiencing a psychic awakening.

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:32.300
In 1547, he returned to Provence, in the town
of Salon, and married a rich widow named Anne

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.300
Ponsarde.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.809
The two would go on to have six children.

00:07:34.809 --> 00:07:39.319
It was around this time that Nostradamus really
got into what he became most famous for: his

00:07:39.319 --> 00:07:40.349
predictions.

00:07:40.349 --> 00:07:44.349
He would bring upon himself a state of trance
by meditating for hours in front of a bowl

00:07:44.349 --> 00:07:47.479
filled with water and herbs, or in front of
a mirror.

00:07:47.479 --> 00:07:51.529
The trance would bring visions, and he would
interpret these into predictions.

00:07:51.529 --> 00:07:56.249
In 1550, Nostradamus wrote down for the first
time these prophecies into an almanac, a popular

00:07:56.249 --> 00:08:00.629
type of book at that time which included advice
for farmers and merchants for the coming year,

00:08:00.629 --> 00:08:02.499
including astrological predictions.

00:08:02.499 --> 00:08:05.909
The success of his almanacs, encouraged Nostradamus.

00:08:05.909 --> 00:08:09.439
The year 1555 saw the publication of his magnum
opus, ‘Les Prophecies’, a collection of

00:08:09.439 --> 00:08:14.809
predictions divided in Centuries, or chapters,
written in the style of four-verse poems,

00:08:14.809 --> 00:08:16.499
known as quatrains.

00:08:16.499 --> 00:08:20.959
These quatrains report Nostradamus’ visions
for the following 2000 years and are written

00:08:20.959 --> 00:08:26.300
in a cryptic style using anagrams, metaphors
and an obscure combination of local French

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:28.740
dialects, Greek, Latin and Italian.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:32.650
Some of his predictions famously anticipated
events such as the great fire of London, the

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:38.800
French Revolution, the advent of Napoleon,
the rise and fall of Hitler, and the 9/11

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:40.820
attacks.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:46.890
Famous prophecies
Here is what Nostradamus wrote about the Fire

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:49.250
of London:
“The blood of the just will be lacking in

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:52.150
London,
Burnt up in the fire of '66:

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:55.030
The ancient Lady will topple from her high
place,

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:57.410
Many of the same sect will be killed.”

00:08:57.410 --> 00:09:03.080
Besides clearly stating the fire of 1666 in
London, the doctor also gets another detail

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:06.060
right: ‘the blood of the just will be lacking’.

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:10.081
Not only the death toll of the fire was relatively
low with eight deaths, but the calamity had

00:09:10.081 --> 00:09:14.820
also the positive effect of burning down millions
of infected rats, thus eliminating the outbreak

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:17.600
of plague that had ravaged the city in previous
years.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:22.380
Now, for the French revolution:
“Songs, chants, and demands will come from

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:26.210
the enslaved
Held captive by the nobility in their prisons

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:31.330
At a later date, brainless idiots
Will take these as divine utterances."

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:36.640
This one is more open to interpretation, although
you find a reference to a rebellion against

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:41.940
nobility, a prison which could be the Bastille
stormed in 1789, and the rise to power of

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:45.760
brainless idiots – possibly the Directorate
during the Terror.

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:50.300
Napoleon also gets one:
"Pau, Nay, Loron, more fire than blood,

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:53.160
Swimming in praise, the great man hurries
to the confluence.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:58.570
He will refuse entry to the magpies,
Pampon and Durrance will confine them.

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:00.950
"
The first three words are an anagram of Napaulon

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:06.240
Roy, which sounds like “Napoleon the King”,
who drew his power from military prowess – fire

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:09.200
– rather than aristocratic origins – blood.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:12.630
There is also a vague reference to magpies
being confined, which has been interpreted

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:17.490
to represent Napoleon’s incarceration of
Popes Pius VI and VII.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:20.760
Napoleon wasn’t the only autocratic conqueror
to be mentioned in the Propheties.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.950
See what you make of this one:
“Beasts ferocious with hunger will cross

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:26.760
the rivers,
The greater part of the battlefield will be

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:27.970
against Hister.

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:30.890
Into a cage of iron will the great one be
drawn,

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:35.840
When the son of Germany obeys no law”
Hister does sound a lot like Hitler, plus

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:37.290
you have Germany in there.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:40.900
And you even get a reference to ferocious
beasts – soldiers or even tanks?

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:44.130
– crossing rivers, in numerical superiority
on a battlefield.

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:48.060
The great one – being Hitler, again – will
be prisoner in a cage of iron, which could

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:50.950
be the bunker where he eventually committed
suicide.

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:53.950
And finally, Nostradamus’ vision of the
9/11 attacks:

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:57.010
“In the city of God there will be a great
thunder

00:10:57.010 --> 00:11:00.630
Two brothers torn apart by Chaos while the
fortress endures

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:04.590
The great leader will succumb
The third big war will begin when the big

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:08.220
city is burning”
Two brothers torn apart: the Twin Towers.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:11.310
The enduring fortress: the Pentagon, which
collapsed only partially.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:15.720
And a ‘third big war’ – on Terror – to
begin straight after.

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:17.520
Could it be any clearer?

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:24.300
Celebrity Status
‘Les Propheties’ has not been out of print

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:28.680
since its first publication, but the book
that solidified Nostradamus’ celebrity status

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:29.830
was the
‘Traité des fardemens et confitures’

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:32.410
Or
‘Treaty on make-up and jams’

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:36.780
This is where he published the plague remedy
I mentioned earlier, as well as recipes for

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:39.200
candied orange peel and cherry preserve.

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:42.110
But the real treat is the ‘love jam’.

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:46.060
The ingredients for this concoction included
ingredients found in every larder nowadays

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:50.280
including cinnamon, cloves, wine, the blood
of seven male sparrows and the tentacles of

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:53.600
an octopus, preserved in honey.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:54.930
But what was it for?

00:11:54.930 --> 00:12:00.170
“If a man were to have a little of it in
his mouth, and while having it in his mouth

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:04.680
kissed a woman, or a woman him, and expelled
it with his saliva, putting some of it in

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:09.300
the other's mouth, it would suddenly cause
... a burning of her heart to perform the

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:12.900
love-act"
We at Biographics do not endorse this as a

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:15.240
method of wooing a lady, preferring to rely
only on our charm, wits and looks.

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:19.590
Nostradamus fame grew and he attracted the
attention of some VIP admirers, such as Queen

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:25.260
Caterina de Medici, wife to King Henri II
and real power behind the scenes of French

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:26.260
politics.

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:30.590
Nostradamus had hinted at some threats to
her family in his almanacs and so the Queen

00:12:30.590 --> 00:12:34.590
summoned him to court appointing him Counselor
and Physician-in-Ordinary to the court.

00:12:34.590 --> 00:12:40.860
In 1556, while serving in this capacity Nostradamus
clarified to her another prophecy from Centuries

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.420
I, which referred to King Henri.

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:46.740
‘Century 1 Quatrain 35
The young lion will overcome the older one,

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:51.700
On the field of combat in a single battle;
He will pierce his eyes through a golden cage,

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:55.190
Two wounds made one, then he dies a cruel
death.’

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:59.880
Despite being warned by Nostradamus to avoid
jousting matches, three years later, King

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:03.860
Henri then aged 41 years old, faced a younger
knight in such a duel.

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:07.620
His opponent’s lance pierced the king’s
visor – shaped as cage - and entered his

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:09.170
brain behind the eye.

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:13.120
After 10 agonizing days the King died of sepsis.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:20.220
Death and Legacy
Nostradamus the doctor unfortunately did not

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:25.250
possess the knowledge to treat the ailment
which cursed him for much of his adult life:

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:26.250
gout.

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:30.660
The condition deteriorated into dropsy, which
is an excessive retention of fluids accumulating

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:34.190
in body cavities, causing heart failure in
its extreme form.

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:39.279
In late June of 1566, Nostradamus called for
his lawyer to draft his last will and testament,

00:13:39.279 --> 00:13:41.350
to the benefit of his wife and children.

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:43.670
On the evening of July the 1st, he told his
secretary Jean de Chavigny,

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:47.160
“You will not find me alive at sunrise.”

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:48.310
Another accurate prophecy.

00:13:48.310 --> 00:13:52.580
The morning after Chavigny found Nostradamus
lying dead next to his bed.

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:57.160
Nostradamus’ greatest legacy is, of course,
his prophetic body of work, which continue

00:13:57.160 --> 00:14:03.120
to puzzle and fascinate scholars and enthusiasts
of the occult worldwide, striving to interpret

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:04.330
his more obscure writings.

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:08.250
We at Biographics want to play our part, too,
and so we will try to find the hidden meaning

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:12.650
behind the recently discovered quatrains which
foreshadow an apocalyptic future.

00:14:12.650 --> 00:14:13.650
Remember the one I read at the beginning?

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:14.650
Here is our translation.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:15.650
From “Les Propheties”, Century nr XIII,
Quatraine nr LXXII

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:16.650
[Script to be read in parallel to text appearing
on screen]

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:17.650
[Original French text appearing as subtitle]
‘In year 19 the Earth is tired’

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:19.620
Anné dix-nouef la Terre est fatiguée
‘A hammer of darkness shall fall like a

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:20.620
plague’

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:23.220
Is this a reference to the Spanish Flu epidemic
of 1919?

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:24.800
Or was he writing about 2019?

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:28.180
Un marteau de tenebre comme peste tombera
‘From the hands of the Prince of thousand

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:29.180
silver windows’

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.560
Silver windows may refer to mirrors, or screens.

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:34.100
A thousand screens – the internet?

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:38.779
Who is the Prince of screens who will cause
this disaster by wielding the hammer of darkness?

00:14:38.779 --> 00:14:42.279
Des mains du Prince des mille fenetres, argentées
‘Later alone, and King among the rubble,

00:14:42.279 --> 00:14:43.420
he will laugh’

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:46.190
The Prince becomes King, sole survivor among
the destruction.

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:47.190
But who?

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:49.820
Puis seul et Roi des décombres, il rira,
That’s him: l’homme qui siffle.

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:51.410
Which is French for

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:52.410
The Whistler
L’homme qui siffle

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:53.410
[screen fades to black, with or without ominous
whistling music]

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:54.410
[After two or three second the black screen
fades back to Simon]

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:56.620
Hello again, I hope you are still watching
and not too spooked by our little prank, here.

00:14:56.620 --> 00:15:01.560
Let me reassure you that there are only 12
Centuries published in the Propheties and

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:04.020
no other quatrains were discovered in Montpelier.

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:09.440
I just wanted to make a point on how easily
in recent years the internet has fostered

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:14.910
unsubstantiated interpretations of Nostradamus’
predictions, or in some cases even circulated

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:19.991
quatrains that were completely made up![TA3]
Take the famous vision of the 9/11, which

00:15:19.991 --> 00:15:20.991
I read earlier.

00:15:20.991 --> 00:15:24.770
That prophecy was a total fake, made up by
a Canadian website to show how easily the

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.720
public can be fooled into believing such predictions.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:34.180
Funnily enough, it was copy and pasted across
the Web and still believed to be genuine.

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:38.620
But the wild interpretation of Nostradamus’
writing style for sensationalistic effect

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:41.100
can be traced back to earlier years.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:44.930
The famous “Hister” quatrain was popularised
by the book ‘The Prophecies of Nostradamus’

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:49.990
by Erika Cheetham, published in 1965, but
her translation from ancient French into English

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:54.010
is either genuinely inaccurate or manipulated
on purpose.

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:58.740
The word “Hister” in the XVI century referred
to the lower Danube region, not to a person.

00:15:58.740 --> 00:16:03.120
The French original contains the word “Germain”,
which Cheetham translated as “German”.

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:07.700
But a more common meaning of the word in French
was “first cousin” or “brother”.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:11.410
In fact here is another translation of the
same prediction by James Randi, the famous

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:14.400
Canadian stage magician and debunker of psychics[TA4]
:

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:17.480
“Beasts mad with hunger will swim across
rivers,

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:20.360
Most of the army will be against the Lower
Danube.

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:22.660
The great one shall be dragged in an iron
cage

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:27.460
When the child brother will observe nothing”
Which may refer to any number of engagements

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:32.830
during the Thirty Years’ War, or the siege
of Vienna by the Ottomans … but as you may

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:37.420
expect prophesising about WWII is far more
enticing.

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:40.020
To conclude, we don’t want you to doubt
all of Nostradamus’ work.

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:48.960
Sure, most of his predictions are vague, obscure,
impossible to decipher or open to exploitative

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:49.960
interpretations.

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:51.500
He may have just made everything up just to
sell books!

00:16:51.500 --> 00:17:19.110
However, it is a fact that some of them contain
accurate depictions of what was then his future.

